    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d411">

                <pb facs="0575" n="479" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg479"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.52/586</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Summerlin</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-03-30"><hi rendition="#italic">March 30,
                        1921</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1552</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department acknowledges the receipt of
                    your despatch, No. 3693, of February 25, 1921,<anchor n="93" xml:id="d411-f1"/>
                    …</p>
                <p>With respect to this law<anchor n="94" xml:id="d411-f2"/> you are directed to
                    point out informally to the appropriate authorities that it does not seem to
                    provide for the establishment of adequate machinery for ascertaining and paying
                    the compensation properly due to owners whose land is expropriated, and that it
                    seems possible that under this law property might be taken without proper
                    provision being made for compensation.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry P.
                            Fletcher</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d411-f1" n="93" xml:id="d411-f1-content">
